  "privacyConsentTitle": "Terms of Service and Privacy Policy",
  "privacyConsentBodyAndroid": "Welcome to {brand}. To provide account sign-in, instant messaging, enterprise collaboration, online customer service, message notifications, and security protection, we need to process necessary information under the Terms of Service and Privacy Policy.\n\nBefore you tap Agree, we will not read clipboard information, initialize JPush/JCore or device-vendor push SDKs, or use those SDKs to access Android ID, OAID, installed-app lists, MAC addresses, or similar information. If you decline for now, we will save that choice; you can continue reading the documents and choose again later.\n\nAfter you agree, to deliver message, customer-service, and incoming-call notifications, JPush/JCore and device-vendor push services may process device model, Android version, app package and version, network type, IP address, Android ID, OAID, push Registration ID, vendor push token, and notification delivery/click data. We have disabled nonessential capabilities including smart push, installed-app lists, MAC, IMEI, IMSI, Wi-Fi lists, auto wake-up, and linked startup.\n\nThe clipboard is accessed only when you actively use copy or paste. Camera, microphone, notification, and other system permissions are requested only when you actively use the corresponding feature. Denying one permission affects only that feature. Please review the full documents below and choose whether to agree.",
  "privacyConsentBodyIos": "Welcome to {brand}. To provide account sign-in, instant messaging, enterprise collaboration, online customer service, message notifications, and security protection, we need to process necessary information under the Terms of Service and Privacy Policy.\n\nBefore you tap Agree, we will not read clipboard information, initialize JPush/JCore, register with Apple Push Notification service (APNs), or obtain push identifiers such as the JPush Registration ID or APNs device token. If you decline for now, we will save that choice; you can continue reading the documents and choose again later.\n\nAfter you agree, to deliver message, customer-service, and incoming-call notifications, we may process iPhone model, iOS version, app package and version, network type, IP address, IDFV, JPush Registration ID, APNs device token, and notification delivery/click data. JPush/JCore connects to the push service; Apple APNs processes the app identifier, device token, and notification payload to deliver system notifications. The current iOS app does not use advertising services or obtain IDFA.\n\nThe clipboard is accessed only when you actively use copy or paste. Camera, microphone, notification, and other system permissions are requested only when you actively use the corresponding feature. Denying one permission affects only that feature. Please review the full documents below and choose whether to agree.",
